---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
const limit = `{
  "error": "usage_limit_reached",
  "message": "Your lifetime free-result credits have been used. Upgrade to continue.",
  "plan": "free",
  "used": 250,
  "limit": 250,
  "upgrade_url": "/pricing"
}`;
---
<DocsLayout title="Barcode API Rate Limits & Monthly Quotas | BarcodeNest" description="Understand BarcodeNest per-minute rate limits, monthly API call allowances, response headers, quota resets and HTTP 429 responses." heading="Rate limits and API allowances." intro="Use response headers and structured 429 errors to keep product lookup traffic within your plan's limits." current="limits">
  <section><h2>Two independent limits</h2><p>BarcodeNest applies a short-window request rate and a billing-period usage allowance. Free has 250 lifetime successful-result credits with no reset. One-time packs have 500 calls each, expiring 30 days after activation. Recurring paid plans have monthly allowances. The request rate limit applies separately.</p><table class="status-table"><thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Allowance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Free</td><td>250 lifetime successful-result credits; no reset</td></tr><tr><td>One-time pack</td><td>500 calls for $4.99; expires after 30 days; no renewal</td></tr><tr><td>Starter</td><td>2,000 calls/month</td></tr><tr><td>Growth</td><td>5,000 calls/month</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
  <section><h2>Response headers</h2><table class="status-table"><thead><tr><th>Header</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>X-RateLimit-Limit</code></td><td>Requests allowed in the rolling 60-second window.</td></tr><tr><td><code>X-RateLimit-Remaining</code></td><td>Capacity remaining in that window.</td></tr><tr><td><code>X-RateLimit-Reset</code></td><td>Unix timestamp when capacity begins to return.</td></tr><tr><td><code>X-Monthly-Quota-Limit</code></td><td>Allowance limit: lifetime matched results on Free, 30-day calls on one-time packs, monthly calls on recurring plans.</td></tr><tr><td><code>X-Monthly-Quota-Remaining</code></td><td>Remaining allowance units.</td></tr><tr><td><code>X-Monthly-Quota-Period</code></td><td>Lifetime on Free; start date for a paid quota period.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
  <section><h2>When a limit is reached</h2><p>Rate-limit and monthly quota enforcement use HTTP <code class="inline-code">429</code>. Short-window rate-limit responses include <code class="inline-code">Retry-After</code>. A monthly usage-limit response includes the current plan, usage, limit, and pricing path.</p><CodeBlock label="Monthly usage limit response" code={limit} language="json" /></section>
  <section><h2>Integration guidance</h2><p>Read the returned headers instead of hard-coding account limits. For transient rate limits, wait for the reset window and use exponential backoff with jitter. Free credits do not reset: upgrade when exhausted. For paid plans, wait until the billing period resets or upgrade.</p><p>Authentication failures, health checks, and account/dashboard requests do not consume the product lookup allowance. Monitor usage in the BarcodeNest dashboard and see <a href="/pricing/">barcode API pricing</a> for plan allowances.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>
